                "><svg width="61" height="56" viewBox="0 0 61 56" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="size-4"><line y1="-3.5" x2="41" y2="-3.5" transform="matrix(0.707107 0.707107 0.707107 -0.707107 5.99609 22.0129)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="7"></line><line y1="-3.5" x2="41" y2="-3.5" transform="matrix(0.718834 -0.695181 -0.695181 -0.718834 25.9961 50.0042)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="7"></line><path d="M30.0751 45.9681L29.6695 0.141299" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="7"></path></svg></span></div></div></nav></dialog><main class="
              flex-1
              bg-primary-soft-white
              pt-[68px]
              desktop:pt-[62px]
            "><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit/plan-your-visit#webpage","url":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit/plan-your-visit","name":"Plan Your Visit to Auckland Art Gallery | Free Entry Guide","description":"Plan your visit to Auckland Art Gallery with free entry details, opening hours, tickets, directions, parking, maps and visitor facilities.","image":"https://cdn.aucklandunlimited.com/aag/assets/media/visit-auckland-art-gallery-thumbnail-web.jpg","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/#website"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit/plan-your-visit#breadcrumb"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit/plan-your-visit#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Visit","item":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Plan your visit","item":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit/plan-your-visit"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit/plan-your-visit#faq","url":"https://www.aucklandartgallery.com/visit/plan-your-visit","name":"Plan Your Visit to Auckland Art Gallery | Free Entry Guide","description":"Plan your visit to Auckland Art Gallery with free entry details, opening hours, tickets, directions, parking, maps and visitor facilities.","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"By bus, train or ferry","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The closest train station to the Gallery is Te Waihorotiu, which is less than 10 minutes away on foot. The&nbsp;Waitematā train station and the Auckland CBD Ferry Terminal are a 15-minute walk away.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nAuckland City Centre is serviced by Link buses to help you get around the CBD.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\n\n\t\n\tThe OuterLink bus stops on Wellesley Street East near the corner of Lorne Street, which is a 1-minute walk to the Gallery.&nbsp;\n\t\n\t\n\tThe CityLink bus stops on Queen Street near the corner of Wellesley Street East, which is a 3-minute walk to the Gallery.&nbsp;\n\t\n\n\nPlan your journey using the Auckland Transport journey planner for the&nbsp;most up to date information about buses, trains and ferries.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nAuckland Transport also has the handy AT Mobile app to help you plan, save and track journeys across Auckland. Download the app from the App Store&nbsp;or the Google Play store."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"By car or taxi","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You&rsquo;ll find many public and private car parks nearby.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nThe closest public car park is Auckland Transport&rsquo;s Victoria Street East car park,&nbsp;which is a 4-minute walk from the Gallery. Rates start from $2.50 per hour on evenings, weekends and public holidays and $5.50 per hour on weekdays.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nParking rates vary based on time and location. Check the Auckland Transport website&nbsp;for more nearby parking options and pricing.&nbsp;\n\nTaxis can pick up and drop off from the loading bays in front of the Gallery on Kitchener Street.&nbsp;"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"By bike","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Auckland City Centre is well connected to other parts of the city by shared paths and dedicated cycleways. Check the Auckland Transport cycleway map for routes and information.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nThere are bike racks for parking directly opposite the Gallery&rsquo;s main entrance on Kitchener Street.&nbsp;&nbsp;"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is free Wi-Fi available at the Gallery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Free Wi-Fi access is available inside the Gallery. It is capped at 1GB of free data per calendar day.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nTo connect:&nbsp;\n\n\n\tEnable Wi-Fi on your device&nbsp;\n\tSelect &lsquo;Auckland Art Gallery&rsquo; &ndash; a login page will automatically open&nbsp;\n\tClick &lsquo;Accept&rsquo; to get online.&nbsp;"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What can I bring into the Gallery with me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We require visitors to check umbrellas, backpacks, shopping bags and large bags into our free cloakroom. To ensure the safety of artworks, the Gallery does not permit visitors to wear bags on their backs in the galleries. The Gallery reserves the right to refuse other items and is not responsible for items held in the cloakroom.&nbsp;"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I eat or drink in the Gallery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No food or drink is permitted in the Gallery, so we recommend a visit to our caf&eacute; on level 1. If you have brought your own lunch, a nice spot to eat is in our amphitheatre behind the Gallery or in Albert Park.&nbsp;\n\nPeople who breastfeed are welcome to feed their babies on any of the public seating in the galleries. If you wish for a more private spot, there is a chair available in the accessible bathroom on the mezzanine floor.&nbsp;\n\nDue to restrictions on food and drink around artworks, bottle feeding for babies or toddlers can only take place in the seating areas in our North Atrium, South Atrium, up on the East Terrace or in the entrance foyer. Likewise, if children need a top-up of food during their visit, please use these areas only. We can assist in guiding you to the right area, so please ask the nearest gallery assistant for help."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I smoke or vape in the Gallery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Smoking and vaping are not permitted anywhere in the Gallery.&nbsp;"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I host an event or party in the Gallery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"While we encourage you to celebrate birthdays and other special events with a visit, large groups should contact the Gallery prior to arrival to see if we can facilitate your request.&nbsp;\n\nPlease note: Parties are not permitted in the galleries or public spaces. Celebrations may only be held in a pre-booked venue within the Gallery. To find out more about venue hire in the Gallery spaces, visit the Auckland Conventions, Venues &amp; Events website."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I photograph or film inside the Gallery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We encourage visitors to capture their favourite works and memories of visiting our exhibitions on display. However, to preserve the artworks and visitor experience, please adhere to the following photography and filming guidelines:\n\n\n\tPhotos and videos can be taken with&nbsp;hand-held cameras for personal use only.\n\tFilming and photography should not disrupt other visitors or be disrespectful to artworks or exhibitions.&nbsp;\n\tLivestreaming is not permitted without the Gallery&#39;s prior permission.&nbsp;\n\tTo reduce the risk of damage to the art, the use of tripods, selfie sticks, external stabilising devices or other camera attachments, flash or additional lighting is not permitted without the permission of the Gallery. A request must be made and granted before such equipment can be used in any Gallery spaces.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\tAny images taken should not be reproduced or displayed on personal or company websites and must not be sold commercially or displayed publicly in any way that disrespects the subjects in the artworks or causes offence to any individuals or groups.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\tPlease follow any &lsquo;No photography&rsquo; signage as this indicates objects, exhibitions or events that cannot be filmed or photographed. This restriction may be for cultural reasons, due to copyright law, privacy, or to protect the people or objects involved.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\n\nIf these guidelines are not followed, you may be asked to stop taking photos and/or filming.&nbsp;\n\nTo request permission for photography or filming, please contact us via marketing@aucklandartgallery.com. Please allow at least 5 working days for a response. Filming and photography are not always possible and may incur a fee. See our copyright&nbsp;and privacy policy for more information.&nbsp;"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I hold my wedding or engagement photoshoot in the Gallery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Gallery does not allow wedding or engagement photography inside the building unless you have hired the venue for a wedding reception or ceremony. To find out more about venue hire in the Gallery spaces, visit the Auckland Conventions, Venues &amp; Events website."}}]}]}</script><section class="
